{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B8mdHrnX6tuAv6oNr3iPHc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Translation of `quic/qlog.h`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Header-only module exposing a single entry point that turns\n4\t//! on per-connection qlog tracing for a QUIC context.  The body\n5\t//! lives in `loglib/autoqlog.c` (a separate target, out of scope\n6\t//! for v1); this module is the picoquic-core stub that links\n7\t//! against it on demand.\n8\t\n9\tuse std::path::Path;\n10\t\n11\tuse crate::{Quic, Result};\n12\t\n13\timpl Quic {\n14\t    /// Enable qlog tracing on this context, writing one qlog file per\n15\t    /// connection into `qlog_dir`.  Installs the unified-logging\n16\t    /// vtable; subsequent connections on this context will stream\n17\t    /// qlog records until the context is dropped.\n18\t    ///\n19\t    /// Both observed call sites guard on the directory being set\n20\t    /// before calling, so the parameter is borrowed (no\n21\t    /// `Option<…>`); the C `int` status (0 / -1) becomes\n22\t    /// `Result<()>`.\n23\t    ///\n24\t    /// C: `int set_qlog(Quic*, char const*)`.\n25\t    pub fn set_qlog(&mut self, _qlog_dir: &(impl AsRef<Path> + ?Sized)) -> Result<()> {\n26\t        todo!()\n27\t    }\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n31\t// Internal qlog encoding helpers (used by qlog_error_test).\n32\t\n33\t/// Write a QLOG-escaped string of `l` bytes from `s`.  Returns `Err` when\n34\t/// the stream had fewer bytes available than `l` (truncation).\n35\t/// C: `qlog_string` in `loglib/qlog.c`.\n36\tpub fn qlog_string<W: std::io::Write>(_out: &mut W, _s: &[u8], _l: usize) -> crate::Result<()> {\n37\t    todo!()\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\t/// Write printable-ASCII QLOG characters from `s` up to `l` bytes.  Returns\n41\t/// `Err` when the stream had fewer bytes than `l`.\n42\t/// C: `qlog_chars` in `loglib/qlog.c`.\n43\tpub fn qlog_chars<W: std::io::Write>(_out: &